  L('m3-2', 'm3', 'Measures of group fairness',
`Let Ŷ be the decision and A the group.

• **Demographic (statistical) parity**: P(Ŷ = 1 | A = a) equal across groups — same approval/selection **rate**. **Disparate impact ratio** = rate of protected group / rate of reference group; the US "**four-fifths (80%) rule**" flags ratios below 0.8.
• **Equal opportunity**: equal **true positive rates** across groups (qualified people are approved equally often).
• **Equalised odds**: equal **TPR and FPR** across groups.
• **Predictive parity**: equal **precision** (PPV) across groups — an approval means the same chance of being good.
• **Calibration within groups**: a score of 0.3 means 30% default probability in every group.
• **Treatment equality**: equal ratio of FN to FP.

Example: approval rates 30% (group B) vs 50% (group A) → disparate impact = 0.6 < 0.8.`,
['Demographic parity: equal selection rates', 'Disparate impact ratio, 80% rule', 'Equal opportunity: equal TPR', 'Equalised odds: equal TPR and FPR', 'Predictive parity: equal precision; calibration']);
