  L('m3-4', 'm3', 'Sources of algorithmic bias and unfairness',
`Bias can enter at every stage of the AI life cycle:

• **Historical bias**: data reflect past discrimination (e.g. historic lending decisions).
• **Representation / sampling bias**: some groups under-represented or absent (e.g. thin-file customers).
• **Measurement bias**: proxies measure the concept unequally (arrests as proxy for crime; cost of care as proxy for illness).
• **Label bias**: labels set by biased human judgements.
• **Aggregation bias**: one model for groups that behave differently.
• **Selection bias / feedback loops**: model decisions determine which data are collected next (rejected applicants never show repayment → **reject inference** problem).
• **Algorithmic/design choices**: objective functions, features, thresholds.
• **Evaluation bias**: benchmarks not representative of the deployed population.
• **Deployment bias**: model used in a context or for a purpose it was not designed for; **automation bias** of users.`,
